<DocsLayout title="Aurora User Guide" description="User-facing guidance and current release documentation availability for Aurora." heading="User guide" eyebrow="DOCUMENTATION / USERS">
<p class="docs-kicker">FOR USERS</p>
<h2>Clear instructions start with a verified release.</h2>
<p>Installation and usage steps must match a specific build, supported hardware and a tested procedure. This website does not currently list a verified public Aurora OS installation release or a verified Lumen browser release.</p>
<div class="docs-callout"><strong>Current availability</strong><p>This page is a guide to finding trustworthy user information. It is not an installation manual. Do not follow unofficial package links or assume that planned features are available.</p></div>
<h2>Before you try a release</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Open <a href="/en/downloads/">Downloads</a> and confirm that an official release artifact is listed.</li>
  <li>Read the release notes and supported hardware or platform information.</li>
  <li>Verify the published checksum and signature using the instructions provided with that release.</li>
  <li>Follow the installation guide for that exact release—not instructions from another version.</li>
  <li>Review known issues and recovery guidance before changing an existing system.</li>
</ol>
<h2>What the complete user guide will cover</h2>
<ul>
  <li>System requirements and supported hardware.</li>
  <li>Installation media verification and installation procedure.</li>
  <li>First boot, device configuration and everyday system use.</li>
  <li>Application installation, permissions and updates.</li>
  <li>Recovery, rollback, accessibility and troubleshooting.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Need an answer now?</h2>
<p>Check the <a href="/en/docs/faq/">FAQ</a> for availability questions, or review the <a href="/en/development/">public development status</a> for evidence and known limitations.</p>
</DocsLayout>
